Q: marker-start &amp; marker-end crop/clip path A: <p>You can use the attributes <code>refX</code> and <code>refY</code> on <code>&lt;marker&gt;</code> to move around the marker in relation to the start and endpoint of the path (see <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/SVG/Reference/Element/marker#attributes" rel="nofollow noreferrer">attributes on <code>&lt;marker&gt;</code></a>).</p>
<p>(I added <code>opacity</code> on the two marker elements to show where the start/end of the path is)</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;svg width="400" height="250"&gt;
  &lt;defs&gt;
    &lt;marker id="hollowRect" orient="auto" overflow="visible"
      markerUnits="userSpaceOnUse" refX="40" refY="20"&gt;
      &lt;rect stroke="#FC5BAC" fill="transparent" width="40" height="40"
        stroke-width="16" opacity=".5" /&gt;
    &lt;/marker&gt;
    &lt;marker id="circle" orient="auto" overflow="visible"
      markerUnits="userSpaceOnUse" refX="0" refY="0"&gt;
      &lt;circle stroke="circle" fill="#FC5BAC" r="30" opacity=".5" /&gt;
    &lt;/marker&gt;
  &lt;/defs&gt;  
  &lt;path d="M 48 30 L 348 30" stroke="red"
    marker-start="url(#hollowRect)" marker-end="url(#circle)"
    stroke-width="20" fill="none" /&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;</code></pre>
